            {
                "entry_id": "89eed528-cb63-3284-9b81-e4073d33ab12",
                "word": "pletsen",
                "pos": "verb",
                "lang_code": "nl",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "32dd3984-a21a-37ba-a019-4b7d4fde3e78",
                        "entry_id": "89eed528-cb63-3284-9b81-e4073d33ab12",
                        "glosses": [
                            "slaan in water"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9f241cc8-8501-40eb-ab77-048c8932cf4d",
                                "sense_id": "32dd3984-a21a-37ba-a019-4b7d4fde3e78",
                                "text": "Ik zou de kilte van die glanzende muurtegels willen voelen, en de ruigte waar het glazuur plaats maakt voor het cement van het voegwerk. Ik zou willen weten wat er schuilgaat achter die deur. Een keldergat, of een gang met donkere arduinen tegels waarop blote voeten zo uitbundig kunnen pletsen?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5238d3c2-e2f2-4f93-a4b1-d335dfdc649b",
                                "sense_id": "32dd3984-a21a-37ba-a019-4b7d4fde3e78",
                                "text": "Al heeft hij ook meteen oog voor de lelijke achterkant van de idylle: ‘Maar een van de ergste gezichten die ik ken in Londen, zijn de kinderen die rondsluipen op deze plek; die in de manden slapen, vechten voor het afval, zich op alles storten wat ze denken te kunnen weggraaien, die duiken onder de wagens en steekkarren, wegspringen voor de politiemannen, en voortdurend met de regen van hun naakte voeten op de Piazza pletsen.' De Standaard 03 FEBRUARI 2012 OM 03:00 UUR"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "87b8249b-b8ae-3c15-ba9c-b333c6f3086d",
                        "entry_id": "89eed528-cb63-3284-9b81-e4073d33ab12",
                        "glosses": [
                            "slaan en zo een hoog geluid produceren"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ea5fc9e9-20e6-4505-ac9e-2216d13a0161",
                                "sense_id": "87b8249b-b8ae-3c15-ba9c-b333c6f3086d",
                                "text": "Bokshandschoenen pletsen op zware bokszakken, die rinkelen aan hun kettingen. Tientallen boksers, van fluo meisjes tot kolossale oud-kampioenen, trainen ongestoord door alsof ze elke dag een Vlaams parlementslid in de ring zien staan."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "62d30104-74c9-49bd-8ccb-8a8f6b9e29bd",
                        "source_entry_id": "89eed528-cb63-3284-9b81-e4073d33ab12",
                        "source_sense_id": "32dd3984-a21a-37ba-a019-4b7d4fde3e78",
                        "source_sense_description": "slaan in water",
                        "target_lang_word": "plash",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "plash",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "840c6c10-8f2b-3892-921f-ffc97d23a334",
                                        "entry_id": "77cd7d86-7bea-3c7d-a9d5-32367b1b4e41",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A small pool of standing water; a puddle."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "UK",
                                            "dialectal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fe6edba8-f977-40cc-8d12-f31d033d8626",
                                                "sense_id": "840c6c10-8f2b-3892-921f-ffc97d23a334",
                                                "text": "Out of the wound the red bloud flowed fresh, / That vnderneath his feet soone made a purple plesh."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d2663f11-7b6a-4bd0-98fc-0a84eec1dc3f",
                                                "sense_id": "840c6c10-8f2b-3892-921f-ffc97d23a334",
                                                "text": "Hereof Aesop framed the Fable of the two Frogs that consulted together in time of drowth (when many plashes that they had repayred to were dry) what was to be done."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "95a01759-bcea-4fdc-aea0-eb08edbf6003",
                                                "sense_id": "840c6c10-8f2b-3892-921f-ffc97d23a334",
                                                "text": "Who were the strugglers, what war did they wage, / Whose savage trample thus could pad the dank / Soil to a plash? [...]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "554dd9a7-f3a4-4a99-8afc-819166e9ae12",
                                                "sense_id": "840c6c10-8f2b-3892-921f-ffc97d23a334",
                                                "text": "These shallow plashes."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7a4ce6d2-b95b-3ef9-adcd-c5d9dc77fc40",
                                        "entry_id": "77cd7d86-7bea-3c7d-a9d5-32367b1b4e41",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A splash, or the sound made by a splash."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2efb08cf-073a-44f9-98c9-cd7f94ada2a9",
                                                "sense_id": "7a4ce6d2-b95b-3ef9-adcd-c5d9dc77fc40",
                                                "text": "Presently a gondola passed along the canal with its slow rhythmical plash, and as we listened we watched it in silence."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e7e2eadb-8546-3c6a-8a25-93abfe2aa2e5",
                                        "entry_id": "77cd7d86-7bea-3c7d-a9d5-32367b1b4e41",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A sudden downpour."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a8a75fe7-2102-440b-9aa2-1a23b8a02586",
                                                "sense_id": "e7e2eadb-8546-3c6a-8a25-93abfe2aa2e5",
                                                "text": "[...] down burst torrents of thick rain and muddied us to the skin. The valley began to run in plashes of water, and Dakhil-Allah urged us across it quickly. [...]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "plash",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1b2e0a94-ef51-32a9-81bb-76f5991c494d",
